    "created_at": "2026-11-12T14:51:33Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-12T14:51:33Z",
    "body": "fix on issue/1241-machine-switch-stale · PR #1254 · pinned by machine_switch::{a_setups,the_documents}_new_machine_{judges_stroke_and_spindle_at_the_post,without_the_rotary_refuses_the_lean,of_another_kind_refuses_the_family} · merges when reviewed\n\n**Trace result: only the display is stale. No path posts on another machine without being checked, so this is not P1-class.** A path generated on machine A was remounted onto machine B, both through the setup's own machine and through the document's. Results on B:\n- Travel: refused by name (`machine TightMill: ... the stroke is -10.000..10.000`).\n- Spindle max rpm: refused (`... above the machine's 1000`).\n- Rotary (tilt-head to VMC 3-axis): refused (`tilts the tool; ... states no tilting rotary`).\n- Kind (mill to Lathe): refused (`cannot run on its setup's ... machine`).\n\nNo refused post writes a file. Undo puts A back and the program posts. Redo and save/reopen keep B's refusal.\n\nThe ops keep reading Ok after a switch on purpose: the M2.3 roomy-one law, pinned by `fixtures.rs::workholding_never_stales_a_fresh_toolpath`. The reasons are recorded in `docs/decisions/1241-machine-switch-live-gate.md`, together with the one-term change (`operation::current_stamp`) if the maintainer wants a switch to show ops as stale anyway. The UI comment quoted in the issue (`setup_mount_pages.rs`) is not on upstream main.\n",
